('combat', 'pylon_speed_attack_speed_pct', 30.0, NULL, 'percent', 'Speed Pylon (docs/proposals/pylons.md 4.3): attack speed. D3: +30% since patch 2.4.0 (Blizzard 2.4.0 notes, Fandom, Icy Veins). The effect reads this live (.dc tunables set moves it); the buff''s tooltip text is baked from it by generate_spells.py (pylons.md, data/pylon_buffs.csv), so a changed number also needs the generator and a client patch to show the new text.'),
('combat', 'pylon_speed_display_id', NULL, 363.0, 'count', 'Pylons and shrines P3 (diablocraft-7h5tr; docs/proposals/pylons.md 6.7 (b)): the gameobject display the Speed Pylon''s object wears. PLACEHOLDER: a stock WoW object the designer picks on dev with .dc pylon spawn <kind> (no Blizzard art, 2026-10-05); it starts at the progress orb''s stock look (363, rifts gr_orb_display_id) as 6.7 says. Read by generate_pylon_objects.py into combat_0054_pylon_objects.sql, so a change needs the generator rerun and that migration applied, not a .dc tunables set'),
('combat', 'pylon_speed_knockup_reach_yards', NULL, 5.0, 'yards', 'Pylons and shrines P2 (diablocraft-eok78; docs/proposals/pylons.md 6.9 (a)): a monster within this distance of the moving wearer is run into. PLACEHOLDER: 6.9''s start, the core''s melee range (NOMINAL_MELEE_RANGE, ObjectDefines.h:47). The designer sets it. Read live (.dc tunables set moves it).'),
('combat', 'pylon_speed_knockup_speed_xy', NULL, 16.0, 'yards per second', 'Pylons and shrines P2 (diablocraft-eok78; docs/proposals/pylons.md 6.9 (a)): the knock-up''s horizontal speed. PLACEHOLDER: 6.9 seeds it at our skills'' knock (ability_knockback_speed_xy 16, ruling 2026-09-29, q-0929-07). Baked into the stock knockback record (generate_spells.py, the effect''s MiscValue in tenths), so a change needs the generator, the spell migration and a client patch.'),
('combat', 'pylon_speed_knockup_speed_z', NULL, 6.0, 'yards per second', 'Pylons and shrines P2 (diablocraft-eok78; docs/proposals/pylons.md 6.9 (a)): the knock-up''s vertical speed. PLACEHOLDER: 6.9 seeds it at our skills'' knock (ability_knockback_speed_z 6, ruling 2026-09-29, q-0929-07). Baked into the stock knockback record (generate_spells.py, the effect''s value in tenths), so a change needs the generator, the spell migration and a client patch.'),
('combat', 'pylon_speed_knockup_tick_ms', NULL, 1000.0, 'milliseconds', 'Pylons and shrines P2 (diablocraft-eok78; docs/proposals/pylons.md 6.9 (a), 5): how often the Speed buff looks for monsters the moving wearer runs into. PLACEHOLDER: D3 publishes none and the plan names no start; 1000 is the start of the other periodic pylon piece (pylon_conduit_pulse_ms, 6.10) and the elite ground zones'' tick (elite_affix_parameters.csv tick_interval). A shorter tick catches more of the monsters run past and costs an area search per tick (pylons.md 5). The designer sets it. Baked into the knock-up record''s period by generate_spells.py, so a change needs the generator, the spell migration and a client patch.'),
('combat', 'pylon_speed_knockup_weapon_damage_pct', NULL, NULL, 'percent', 'Pylons and shrines P2 (diablocraft-eok78; docs/proposals/pylons.md 6.9 (a)): a monster knocked up takes a hit of this much weapon damage through the damage formula. ALEX SETS IT: D3 says the knock-up damages them, the amount not published (D5); 6.9: the row starts empty, so the knock-up deals no damage until a number is here. Read live (.dc tunables set moves it).'),
('combat', 'pylon_speed_movement_pct', 80.0, NULL, 'percent', 'Speed Pylon (docs/proposals/pylons.md 4.3, 6.3): movement speed, past the usual cap (a Temporary contribution, which the sheet does not cap). D3: +80% (in-game text, Fandom); Maxroll, Icy Veins and Bagstone say 100%, not taken. The effect reads this live (.dc tunables set moves it); the buff''s tooltip text is baked from it by generate_spells.py (pylons.md, data/pylon_buffs.csv), so a changed number also needs the generator and a client patch to show the new text.'),
('combat', 'pylon_speed_seconds', 60.0, NULL, 'seconds', 'Speed Pylon (docs/proposals/pylons.md 6.3): how long the buff lasts. D3: 60 s since patch 2.1.2.'),
('combat', 'resource_pulse_ms', NULL, 100.0, 'milliseconds', 'diablocraft-dupme (ruling 2026-10-14: "resource power is coming back in chunks. In D3 it''s a smooth flowing increase/decrease"): how often the module pays a class resource stored on Rage or Runic Power (Fury, Spirit) its regeneration and its out-of-combat decay, in place of the core''s 2-second tick (src/stats/dc_resource_pulse.cpp). Rates never change with it: each pulse pays rate x elapsed and carries the fraction. No D3 number (D3''s bar moves every frame). PLACEHOLDER: 100 (ten steps a second) is the brief''s engineering figure; the designer sets it. Smaller is smoother and sends more power updates. Read live (.dc tunables set moves it); 0 pays every player update.'),
('combat', 'revive_body_limit', 3.0, NULL, 'count', 'diablocraft-uxps (docs/decisions.md 2026-10-09, the designer: D3 patch 2.0.1 rule). Most revives at the body (Revive at Corpse) in a row outside a Greater Rift before only Revive at Checkpoint or in Town are left; inside a Greater Rift there is no limit. Any revive at the checkpoint or in town starts the count again. D3 published 3: Blizzard patch 2.0.1 notes, 2014-02-25 (https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/12671560/patch-2-0-1-now-live): "Players may only resurrect at their body a maximum of three times in a row". Blank or 0 means no limit'),
('combat', 'revive_burst', NULL, 10.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-revive-choices-server: DCREVIVE (the death window: Revive here / in town / at rift start) requests a player may send at once; the same 10 the designer set for every window route (artisan_burst, jeweler_burst, q-0930-49); his to change. Blank would mean the route refuses every request (docs/contracts/window-bridge.md, Budget).'),
('combat', 'revive_per_second', NULL, 5.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-revive-choices-server: DCREVIVE tokens per second a player gets back; the same 5 the designer set for every window route (artisan_per_second, jeweler_per_second, q-0930-49); his to change. Blank would mean the route refuses every request (docs/contracts/window-bridge.md, Budget).'),
('combat', 'revive_town_spread_yards', NULL, 10.0, 'yards', 'diablocraft-uxps (docs/decisions.md 2026-10-09, the designer: town arrivals spread round the hub''s spawn, logins not included). The designer set 10 and tested it on dev 2026-10-10 (diablocraft-wt1k): radius of the disc round world_hub_points.csv spawn in which a Revive in Town (and a living player the core would send to a graveyard) lands, on dry ground the spawn can see. Blank or 0 means everyone lands on the spawn itself'),
('combat', 'shrine_blessed_damage_taken_pct', 25.0, NULL, 'percent', 'Blessed Shrine (docs/proposals/pylons.md 4.3): damage taken is this much lower (a Temporary specific reduction). D3: 25% (Blizzard''s guide, Fandom; the shrine is now called Protection, the buff keeps Blessed). The effect reads this live (.dc tunables set moves it); the buff''s tooltip text is baked from it by generate_spells.py (pylons.md, data/pylon_buffs.csv), so a changed number also needs the generator and a client patch to show the new text.'),
