('rifts', 'bounty_click_channel_ms', 4000.0, NULL, 'milliseconds', 'diablocraft-dm9vg.2: a Click objective''s channel (maxroll bounties: ''Clicking on an objective will start a 4 second channel, that is interrupted by damage, unless you are immune to Crowd Control''). Read when the server loads its spells, as town_portal_cast_ms: a change needs a restart, and a length with no SpellCastTimes row keeps the spell''s own'),
('rifts', 'bounty_click_objectives_max', 6.0, NULL, 'count', 'diablocraft-dm9vg.1: most objectives a Click bounty draws from its spots (maxroll bounties: ''multiple (3 to 6) objectives''); a bounty never draws more than bounties.csv lists for it. Read when a board is drawn'),
('rifts', 'bounty_click_objectives_min', 3.0, NULL, 'count', 'diablocraft-dm9vg.1: fewest objectives a Click bounty draws from its spots (maxroll bounties: ''you have multiple (3 to 6) objectives in the same zone''). Read when a board is drawn'),
('rifts', 'bounty_kill_monster_count', NULL, NULL, 'count', 'diablocraft-dm9vg.1: monsters a Kill bounty asks for besides its named Unique (maxroll bounties: ''kill a fixed number of monsters within a zone plus Unique monster''; D3 publishes no number). Blank or 0: the Unique alone. Read when a board is drawn, so a change reaches the next draw'),
('rifts', 'bounty_travel_cast_ms', NULL, 1500.0, 'milliseconds', 'diablocraft-dm9vg.10: the bounty travel cast from the open world (ruling 2026-10-12: Town Portal''s cast length as the default, town_portal_cast_ms); from the Sanctum travel stays instant. Read when the server loads its spells, as town_portal_cast_ms: a change needs a restart, and a length with no SpellCastTimes row keeps the spell''s own'),
('rifts', 'close_announce_final_seconds', NULL, 10.0, 'seconds', 'audit row 90; the mark from which every remaining second is announced. No origin found'),
('rifts', 'close_announce_first_seconds', NULL, 30.0, 'seconds', 'audit row 89; the first countdown mark announced while the close runs. No origin found'),
('rifts', 'close_countdown_ms', NULL, 30000.0, 'milliseconds', 'audit row 92 RIFT_CLOSE_MS; 09-rifts 2 step 6 (ruling 2026-09-07), called "the designer''s existing 2 decision" in 09 7'),
('rifts', 'cluster_min_spacing_yards', NULL, NULL, 'yards', 'Monster spawning S2 return (diablocraft-nwjf; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.3 ''never two on one spot''): the least distance between two members of one cluster; a spot closer than this to one already placed is drawn again. PLACEHOLDER: blank until the designer sets it, and blank means only that no two share a point. The members stand at random points within the radius (uniform over the disc), not on a spiral.'),
('rifts', 'cluster_radius_small_yards', NULL, 5.0, 'yards', 'Monster spawning S1 (diablocraft-dt7c; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.3): radius a small cluster''s members stand within round the anchor; larger clusters take radius x sqrt(bodies / 4). SEED, ALEX SETS IT: today''s minion_spread (elite_affix_parameters.csv)'),
('rifts', 'copy_cap_alteracmountains', NULL, 20.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-hyoic.8 (bounty acts A5; plan docs/research/bounty-acts.md 7, the per-zone cap starts at 20 like the first set''s, a tunable per zone): how many strangers Alterac Mountains takes inside one copy of map 752 before the router opens or picks another. A party goes past it to stay together (up to the party size minus one more). Read by dc_open_rift.cpp when a trip is routed.'),
