('rifts', 'gr_xp_mid_last_level', 70.0, NULL, 'level', 'Greater Rift part 8 (diablocraft-yxsa; docs/briefs/greater-rifts-brief.md part 8, docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md card 6b, ruling 2026-10-04): the last level of the x gr_xp_per_level_mid band (greater_rifts.csv xp_gain_per_rank: x1.08 per rank GR26-70); the next band, x gr_xp_per_level_high, runs to the Greater Rift cap'),
('rifts', 'gr_xp_per_level_high', 1.05, NULL, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 8 (diablocraft-yxsa; docs/briefs/greater-rifts-brief.md part 8, docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md card 6b, ruling 2026-10-04): Guardian XP times this per level above gr_xp_mid_last_level. greater_rifts.csv xp_gain_per_rank: x1.05 per rank GR71-150'),
('rifts', 'gr_xp_per_level_mid', 1.08, NULL, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 8 (diablocraft-yxsa; docs/briefs/greater-rifts-brief.md part 8, docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md card 6b, ruling 2026-10-04): Guardian XP times this per level above the table up to gr_xp_mid_last_level. greater_rifts.csv xp_gain_per_rank (maxroll.gg/d3/resources/greater-rifts, pasted by ruling 2026-09-12)'),
('rifts', 'gr_xp_table_last_level', 25.0, NULL, 'level', 'Greater Rift part 8 (diablocraft-yxsa; docs/briefs/greater-rifts-brief.md part 8, docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md card 6b, ruling 2026-10-04): the last Greater Rift level of the hand-picked XP table gr_xp_level_02 .. gr_xp_level_NN (greater_rifts.csv xp_gain_per_rank: GR1-25 hand-picked per rank). The rows are the table; the code reads one row per level up to this one'),
('rifts', 'greater_rift_keystone_cost', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Greater Rift part 2 (diablocraft-0uyw; docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md ruling 2, ruling 2026-10-03; greater_rifts.csv keystone_upgrade_rule): Greater Rift Keystones taken from the OPENER when a Greater Rift starts; the other members pay none'),
('rifts', 'greater_rift_max_level', NULL, 75.0, 'level', 'Greater Rift part 1 (diablocraft-kv2d): the highest Greater Rift level, which no unlock, opener''s level or stored character level passes (a stored level above it reads as it). 75 since the designer, card q-1006-01 (docs/decisions.md 2026-10-06 ''Greater Rift levels and difficulty'', diablocraft-e4zf): Greater Rifts stop at 75 ''while I look for a way to go past 75''; was 150 (docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md ruling 1, 2026-10-03). Torment XVI''s solo Greater Rift 75 (difficulty_tiers.csv) is the highest level anything asks for'),
('rifts', 'greater_rift_start_level', NULL, 1.0, 'level', 'Greater Rift part 1 (diablocraft-kv2d; docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md ruling 1, ruling 2026-10-03): the Greater Rift level every character starts with unlocked'),
('rifts', 'guardian_ability_repeat_ms', NULL, 11000.0, 'milliseconds', 'audit row 71 GUARDIAN_REPEAT_MS; as guardian_first_ability_ms'),
('rifts', 'guardian_base_life', NULL, 2390220.0, 'count', '64-bit Life (diablocraft-12in; the designer''s card q-1007-04, decisions.md 2026-10-08 D2): every Rift Guardian, Nephalem and Greater, takes this one base Life instead of its stock template''s, as Diablo III normalized the 27 to one pool (monster_base_stats.csv Rift Guardian row; D3 publishes no number). Tier or Greater Rift level and party multiply it as they multiply any creature''s base. SEED, ALEX SETS IT: 2,390,220 is the median of the 27 stock templates (big-life-2026-10-07 report 1.1); the stock range is 8,300 to 14,154,175. Read when the Guardian is scaled, so a change applies to Guardians spawned after `.dc tunables reload`'),
('rifts', 'guardian_clear_range_yards', 100.0, NULL, 'yards', 'from greater_rifts.csv:item=rift_guardian_spawn_rule.guardian_clear_range_yards, this row''s own notes column: "all other monsters within 100 yards die and despawn". Audit row 66'),
('rifts', 'guardian_first_ability_ms', NULL, 6000.0, 'milliseconds', 'audit row 70 GUARDIAN_FIRST_MS; guardian cooldowns are NOT PUBLISHED in rift_guardian_stats.csv'),
('rifts', 'guardian_frenzy_haste_pct', 50.0, NULL, 'percent', 'audit row 72 GUARDIAN_FRENZY_HASTE. D3 value sourced by Gemini (literal-audit-sources-2.md row 72): rift_guardian_stats.csv:18 and Maxroll give Bloodmaw''s Frenzy as +50% Attack Speed. The code carried 30; leaving value blank adopts the published 50, and the designer can set it back'),
('rifts', 'guardian_leap_damage_multiplier', NULL, 4.0, 'multiplier', 'audit row 68 GUARDIAN_LEAP; leap or charge damage on the same scale as guardian_nova_damage_multiplier'),
('rifts', 'guardian_nova_damage_multiplier', NULL, 3.0, 'multiplier', 'audit row 67 GUARDIAN_NOVA; nova damage as a multiple of the guardian''s average swing. rift_guardian_stats.csv marks every guardian damage_pct NOT PUBLISHED'),
('rifts', 'guardian_nova_radius_yards', NULL, 15.0, 'yards', 'audit row 69 GUARDIAN_NOVA_RADIUS; rift_guardian_stats.csv gives Cold Snap''s nova as 60 yd and Agnidox''s as screen-wide, neither is 15, so this is ours'),
('rifts', 'guardian_spawn_range_yards', NULL, 30.0, 'yards', 'audit row 65 GUARDIAN_SPAWN_RANGE; 09-rifts 2 step 4. Gemini found no published guardian spawn distance (literal-audit-sources-2.md row 65), so it is ours'),
('rifts', 'instance_reservation_ms', NULL, 120000.0, 'milliseconds', 'audit row 93 RESERVATION_MS; how long a created instance is held for its party. No origin found'),
('rifts', 'monster_progress_default_points', 1.0, NULL, 'count', 'Monster spawning S3 (diablocraft-43j0; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.9.4): D3 progress points a kill adds when its monster has no row in gr_monster_progress.csv: the roster monsters whose warpath_name is none, and a creature that is not a roster monster (a Guardian, a family summon that counts). D3''s median monster is 1.0 point. SEED, ALEX SETS IT: the plan counts them at 1.0 until he sets them. A kill adds points x 100 hundredths to the bar (650 points = 65,000).'),
('rifts', 'nr_orb_champion_count', NULL, 3.0, 'count', 'Monster spawning S1 (diablocraft-dt7c; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.9.4; ruling 2026-10-08, decisions.md b4171f62): progress orbs a Nephalem Rift champion pack drops. Ruling 2026-10-09 q-1008-11 (decisions.md, built in diablocraft-xgms): 3, as a Greater Rift champion pack. D3 publishes "3 or 4" a pack for Nephalem Rifts, not which'),
('rifts', 'nr_orb_display_id', NULL, 9701.0, 'count', 'Monster spawning S1 (diablocraft-dt7c; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.9.4): the gameobject display of the orange Nephalem orb, beside the purple gr_orb_display_id. The designer picked 9701, the Flame Sphere (a bare orange sphere, spells/firebomb_missle), from the .dc orbrow row on dev (2026-10-16, diablocraft-ivtf5). Read by generate_rifts.py into rifts_0031_nr_orb_look.sql (rifts_0020 is applied and frozen), so a change needs the generator rerun and that migration applied, not a .dc tunables set'),
('rifts', 'nr_orb_lift_yards', NULL, 0.6, 'yards', 'The Nephalem orb''s height (diablocraft-ivtf5): the Flame Sphere is centred on its model''s origin, so the orb is summoned this far above the ground, the 0.6 the orb row used (dc_orb_pick.h). The Greater orb is a floor aura and is not lifted. Read by dc_gr_progress.cpp when the orb drops; .dc tunables reload applies it'),
('rifts', 'nr_orb_points', NULL, 6.5, 'count', 'Monster spawning S1 (diablocraft-dt7c; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.9.4): D3 progress points one Nephalem orb adds. Ruling 2026-10-09 q-1008-11 (decisions.md, built in diablocraft-xgms): 1% of the 650-point bar (the Diablo Wiki), 6.5; Blizzard published no number'),
('rifts', 'nr_orb_rare_count', NULL, 4.0, 'count', 'Monster spawning S1 (diablocraft-dt7c; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.9.4): progress orbs a Nephalem Rift rare pack drops. Ruling 2026-10-09 q-1008-11 (decisions.md, built in diablocraft-xgms): 4, as a Greater Rift rare pack'),
('rifts', 'nr_orb_scale', NULL, 0.15, 'multiplier', 'The Nephalem orb''s size (diablocraft-ivtf5): the Flame Sphere model (9701) is 4.6 yards across at 1, and the orb row (.dc orbrow, dc_orb_pick.h) brought it to about a globe''s size, radius 0.35 yards, at 0.15. Read by generate_rifts.py into the template''s size in rifts_0031_nr_orb_look.sql, so a change needs the generator rerun and a new migration, not a .dc tunables set'),
('rifts', 'open_portal_ms', NULL, 800.0, 'milliseconds', 'audit rows 83 and 102 (OPEN_PORTAL_MS and dc_shatter.cpp''s PORTAL_MS, one row for both). docs/research/obelisk-shatter.md 6 timeline, t = 0.8 s'),
('rifts', 'open_rift_entry_alteracmountains_o', NULL, 5.37858, 'radians', 'Alterac Mountains on the rift copy (map 752; diablocraft-hyoic.8, ruling 2026-10-12 via the Architect): the o of the zone''s entrance point. The stock .tele spot ''AlteracMountains'' (game_tele id 22, map 0, base SQL game_tele.sql), a place to start until the Zone Survey page replaces it.'),
('rifts', 'open_rift_entry_alteracmountains_x', NULL, 370.763, 'yards', 'Alterac Mountains on the rift copy (map 752; diablocraft-hyoic.8, ruling 2026-10-12 via the Architect): the x of the zone''s entrance point. The stock .tele spot ''AlteracMountains'' (game_tele id 22, map 0, base SQL game_tele.sql), a place to start until the Zone Survey page replaces it.'),
('rifts', 'open_rift_entry_alteracmountains_y', NULL, -491.355, 'yards', 'Alterac Mountains on the rift copy (map 752; diablocraft-hyoic.8, ruling 2026-10-12 via the Architect): the y of the zone''s entrance point. The stock .tele spot ''AlteracMountains'' (game_tele id 22, map 0, base SQL game_tele.sql), a place to start until the Zone Survey page replaces it.'),
