('rifts', 'open_rift_wall_01_r', NULL, 25.0, 'yards', 'Un''Goro rift copy wall spot 1 (diablocraft-jj6n; ruling 2026-10-09, card q-1008-16): the radius of the sphere. 25 yards is the distance the research clustered its candidates within (open-world-rifts.md 2.3), so one spot covers its cluster; the designer sets it. 0 switches the spot off.'),
('rifts', 'open_rift_wall_01_x', NULL, -8273.7, 'yards', 'Un''Goro rift copy wall spot 1 (diablocraft-jj6n; ruling 2026-10-09, card q-1008-16): a place where the navmesh lets a player walk on foot from the entrance to the zone''s edge (2 portals, slope 39.7; lowest slope of the crossing, degrees), a navmesh crossing that is not among the research''s 29 candidates. Found by the walk-reach scan in docs/test-diablocraft-jj6n.md; NOT confirmed in game. The x of the spot''s centre on map 751. A spot is a sphere: a player inside it is bounced to the entrance like the zone edge (dc_open_rift.cpp). Spots are numbered from 01 with no gap (the list ends at the first spot with a blank row); to switch one off set its _r to 0.'),
