('rifts', 'open_rubble_ms', NULL, 200.0, 'milliseconds', 'audit rows 82 and 101 (OPEN_RUBBLE_MS and dc_shatter.cpp''s RUBBLE_MS, one row for both). docs/research/obelisk-shatter.md 6 timeline, t = 0.2 s; one of the designer''s four shatter settings'),
('rifts', 'open_zone_area_max_yards', NULL, 120.0, 'yards', 'Monster spawning S1 (diablocraft-dt7c; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.5.2): an open-zone area is at most this far across (dungeons use rift_survey.csv area_max_yards, 40). The plan gave no number: the designer set it on 2026-10-16 (card q-1016-24, diablocraft-71kk3). Read by S6'),
('rifts', 'open_zone_spacing_yards', NULL, 40.0, 'yards', 'Monster spawning S1 (diablocraft-dt7c; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.5.2): least distance between sampled anchors on an open zone''s thin ground. The plan gave no number: the designer set it on 2026-10-16 (card q-1016-24, diablocraft-71kk3). Read by the open zones part (S6)'),
('rifts', 'patrol_record_step_yards', NULL, 4.0, 'yards', 'Monster spawning S5 (diablocraft-tyt6; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.6): `.dc patrol record` keeps a point of the walk each time the designer has moved this far (straight line) from the last point kept. 4 is ALEX''S VALUE (docs/decisions.md 2026-10-09 Patrol tunables, diablocraft-tpji)'),
('rifts', 'patrol_share_pct', NULL, 20.0, 'percent', 'Monster spawning S1 (diablocraft-dt7c; docs/proposals/monster-spawning.md 3.6): the share of picked anchors with a route that hold a patrol. 20 is ALEX''S VALUE (docs/decisions.md 2026-10-09 Patrol tunables, diablocraft-tpji). Read by the patrols part (S5, dc_rift_spawn.h): blank is 0, no patrol walks'),
('rifts', 'pylon_gr_base_chance_pct', 1.0, NULL, 'percent', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (6.5 (a), D10): in a Greater Rift a spot rolls once, when the first player comes near, at this chance right after a pylon (or at the start). Maxroll, Greater Rift Mechanics 2023-09-14: ''This chance is reset to ~1% after spawning a Pylon'''),
('rifts', 'pylon_gr_check_ms', NULL, 1000.0, 'milliseconds', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (6.5 (a)): how often a Greater Rift floor looks for a player near an unrolled spot. Ours (D3 publishes none); the look is a few distance checks, so a second costs nothing, and a longer wait lets a player run past a spot; ruling 2026-10-11 (decisions 1551ce0e): yes to the 1000 ms check'),
('rifts', 'pylon_gr_check_yards', 75.0, NULL, 'yards', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (6.5 (a), D10): a Greater Rift spot rolls when the first player comes within this distance. Maxroll, Greater Rift Mechanics 2023-09-14: ''Pylon spawn locations are checked when you are 75 yards away from them'''),
('rifts', 'pylon_gr_full_chance_progress_pct', 50.0, NULL, 'percent', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (6.5 (a), D10): the progress since the last pylon, as a share of the bar, at which the chance has risen in a line to 100%. Maxroll, Greater Rift Mechanics 2023-09-14: ''scales linearly up to ~50% progress where your chance to find a Pylon on the next spot is 100%'' (the players'' curve is +3% per 1%, 6.5 (b), not taken)'),
('rifts', 'pylon_gr_max_per_run', 4.0, NULL, 'count', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (6.5 (a), D10): the most pylons a Greater Rift run holds, an unclicked one counted; none rolls after the Guardian is up. Maxroll, Greater Rift Mechanics 2023-09-14: ''It is only possible to spawn up to four Pylons per Greater Rift'''),
('rifts', 'pylon_min_spacing_yd', NULL, 60.0, 'yards', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (ruling 2026-10-11, decisions 1551ce0e): no two placed objects, pylon or shrine, nearer than this, in both rift kinds. A Nephalem spot that rolls a hit within it of another placed or already rolled object is skipped at the floor-open roll; a Greater Rift spot that does is dropped and the chance is kept, not stored. Seed 60, the designer''s. 0 keeps nothing apart. ALEX SETS IT'),
('rifts', 'pylon_nr_pylon_chance_pct', NULL, 5.0, 'percent', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (diablocraft-0x640; docs/proposals/pylons.md 6.5 (c), ruling 2026-10-11): in a Nephalem Rift every spot of a floor rolls once when the floor opens, a pylon at this chance. D3 publishes no Nephalem count (D9), so it is ours; the start gives about one pylon a floor on the plan''s 22 spots (about 0.8 on the 15 the survey measured). ALEX SETS IT'),
('rifts', 'pylon_nr_pylons_max', NULL, 2.0, 'count', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (6.5 (c)): a Nephalem floor holds at most this many pylons; surplus rolls are dropped at random. Ours. ALEX SETS IT'),
('rifts', 'pylon_nr_pylons_min', NULL, 0.0, 'count', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (6.5 (c)): a Nephalem floor holds at least this many pylons; a floor that rolls fewer is topped up at random spots. 0: none needed. The safeguard shape the designer gave the elite packs (q-1008-06 4.9). ALEX SETS IT'),
('rifts', 'pylon_nr_shrine_chance_pct', NULL, 13.0, 'percent', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (6.5 (c)): the same roll, a shrine at this chance (a spot that rolls neither stays empty). Ours, under Maxroll''s ''often 5+'' shrines a floor (D9). ALEX SETS IT'),
('rifts', 'pylon_nr_shrines_max', NULL, 5.0, 'count', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (6.5 (c)): a Nephalem floor holds at most this many shrines. Ours, Maxroll''s ''often 5+'' (D9) as the ceiling. ALEX SETS IT'),
('rifts', 'pylon_nr_shrines_min', NULL, 0.0, 'count', 'Pylons and shrines P4 (6.5 (c)): a Nephalem floor holds at least this many shrines. 0: none needed. ALEX SETS IT'),
('rifts', 'rift_max_floors', NULL, 10.0, 'count', 'Rift floors F2 (docs/proposals/rift-floors.md 4.3 item 5 and 6.1, ruling 2026-10-08 card q-1008-08: a cap, seeded at D3''s most): a run opens at most this many floors, the last has no exit portal. D3 rolls 1 to 10 per rift (Blizzard''s 2013 panel); ALEX SETS IT'),
('rifts', 'shatter_preview_clear_ms', NULL, 1000.0, 'milliseconds', 'audit row 103 CLEAR_MS; docs/research/obelisk-shatter.md 6 timeline, t = 1.0 s (stalker despawns)'),
